(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// sys.monitoring's call-family events (PEP 669; queue 220, Python/instrumentation.c and Python/legacy_tracing.c of"] [4 1 "// CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement): the tools' registry (use_tool_id, free_tool_id, clear_tool_id, get_tool),"] [5 1 "// their global events (set_events, get_events) and callbacks (register_callback), and the events a profiler needs:"] [6 1 "// PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW, PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD, PY_UNWIND at a frame's start and end (runFrames), CALL, C_RETURN"] [7 1 "// and C_RAISE at the call sites of the loop and of compiled code (eval.go, aot.go). sys.setprofile is the legacy tool"] [8 1 "// over them (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID 6), as legacy_tracing.c makes it. _lsprof (builtins_lsprof.go) is a tool."] [9 1 "//"] [10 1 "// Off, an event costs one load of monEvents (0 when no tool has an event) and a branch. A callback runs with the thread's"] [11 1 "// tracing count up (tstate->tracing): no event fires inside it. Not built: the local events (set_local_events,"] [12 1 "// get_local_events record nothing), LINE, INSTRUCTION, JUMP, BRANCH*, RAISE, RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED and"] [13 1 "// STOP_ITERATION never fire (settrace's are 219's). Since queue 274b a callback's DISABLE turns its event off at the"] [14 1 "// location for the tool (the code object and the offset; an event that cannot be disabled raises ValueError and loses"] [15 1 "// its callback), restart_events turns them on again, C_RETURN and C_RAISE follow CALL as CPython's ancillary events,"] [16 1 "// and sys.monitoring's C API (PyMonitoring_EnterScope, the _PyMonitoring_Fire*Event functions) is pyctypes' over"] [17 1 "// MonitoringTools and MonitoringCall below."] [18 1 "// CALL's instruction_offset is 2 x the IR's instruction (f_lasti's unit)."] [20 1 "// the events' numbers (the bit index of sys.monitoring.events' values)"] [32 2 "// monProfileTool is the legacy profiler's tool (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID)"] [37 1 "// monCallFamily are the events a profiler uses (legacy_tracing.c's for sys.setprofile)"] [41 1 "// monTool is a tool's registration: its name (nil: free), its global events, its callbacks by event."] [46 2 "// native, for the legacy profiler: called in place of cb"] [52 2 "// monEvents is the union of every tool's global events: the hooks' one load"] [54 2 "// monMissing and monDisable are sys.monitoring.MISSING and DISABLE"] [57 2 "// monTracing are the threads running a callback (tstate->tracing); under the GIL"] [59 2 "// monVersion is the interpreter's instrumentation version (queue 274b, the C API's PyMonitoring_EnterScope): raised"] [60 2 "// when a tool's global events change (monSeen: the events at the last change), as _PyMonitoring_SetEvents does"] [65 1 "// monUpdate recomputes monEvents, and breakMonitor in the eval breaker: a frame's start checks the breaker alone, so"] [66 1 "// its PY_START costs nothing while no tool has an event."] [84 1 "// monEventBit is the bit of a tool's events that has it fire ev: CALL's for C_RETURN and C_RAISE, the ancillary"] [85 1 "// events (CPython's tools for them are CALL's)."] [93 1 "// monFire calls the tools' callbacks of event ev with args; the first error is returned (raised where the event is)."] [126 4 "// call_instrumentation_vector (queue 274b): DISABLE turns the event off at this location for the tool until"] [127 4 "// restart_events; the other events cannot be disabled, their callback is removed"] [141 1 "// monSite is an instrumented location: a code object, an event and its offset (DISABLE's unit)."] [148 1 "// monDisabled are the locations DISABLE turned off, by tool (restart_events clears them)."] [151 1 "// monSiteOf is ev's location in f (its offset the callback's second argument), and whether ev is a local"] [152 1 "// (instrumented) event DISABLE can turn off (PY_MONITORING_IS_INSTRUMENTED_EVENT: the events below RAISE)."] [170 1 "// monEnter is a frame's start in runFrames: PY_THROW for an exception thrown into a generator's frame, PY_START for a"] [171 1 "// frame at its first instruction, else PY_RESUME."] [190 1 "// monLeave is a frame's return of v in runFrames: PY_YIELD when it is suspended, else PY_RETURN."] [202 1 "// monUnwind is a frame left by exc (PY_UNWIND); a callback's error replaces the exception."] [215 1 "// monCall is CALL before a call of callable from f, arg0 its first argument (self for a method) or nil."] [226 1 "// monCReturn is C_RETURN or C_RAISE after a call of callable, not a Python function, from f: the call's result, or a"] [227 1 "// callback's error."] [245 1 "// monCallC is a call of a callable that is not a Python function from f with monitoring on: CALL, the call, then"] [246 1 "// C_RETURN or C_RAISE."] [259 1 "// isPyFunction is whether a call of o runs a Python frame (a function, or a bound method of one): no C events."] [272 1 "// the legacy profiler (sys.setprofile): each thread's function, and how many threads have one"] [287 1 "// setProfile is _PyEval_SetProfile for t: fn None removes it."] [297 1 "// profileCFunc is the C function a CALL's callable stands for (legacy_tracing.c's sys_profile_call_or_return): a"] [298 1 "// built-in function or method itself, a method descriptor bound to its first argument; nil for any other callable."] [312 1 "// builtinOwner is the type in arg0's type's MRO whose dict holds b (a method descriptor's d_type), or nil."] [325 1 "// profileEvent is the legacy tool's callback: the thread's profile function called as (frame, event, arg); an error"] [326 1 "// removes it (sys.setprofile(None)) and is raised."] [360 1 "// newMonitoringModule is sys.monitoring."] [475 3 "// monitoring_set_events_impl (queue 274b): C_RETURN and C_RAISE are not kept, they follow CALL (call_one_instrument's"] [476 3 "// tools for them are CALL's); BRANCH is BRANCH_LEFT and BRANCH_RIGHT"] [517 3 "// _PyMonitoring_RestartEvents (queue 274b): every disabled location on again"] [526 1 "// monCallSite is a call site's monitoring (queue 220): CALL fired; a callable that is no Python function called here"] [527 1 "// with C_RETURN or C_RAISE after it (done true, its result); a Python function's call left to the site (done false)."] [544 1 "// callStackMon is callStack's monitoring: monCallSite over the call's callable and arguments on f's stack, which a C"] [545 1 "// callable's call pops."] [570 1 "// The C API's view of the monitors (queue 274b; Python/instrumentation.c's PyMonitoring_EnterScope and"] [571 1 "// capi_call_instrumentation, CPython 3.14.10): the C half is pyctypes' (capi_monitoring.go)."] [573 1 "// monEventNames are instrumentation.c's event_names, by event number."] [578 1 "// MonitoringVersion is the instrumentation version PyMonitoring_EnterScope compares with a scope's."] [581 1 "// MonitoringTools is _Py_GlobalMonitors' tools[ev]: the tools whose global events have ev. An extension's tool's events"] [582 1 "// as set_events stores them (monitoring_set_events_impl: BRANCH as BRANCH_LEFT and BRANCH_RIGHT, C_RETURN and C_RAISE"] [583 1 "// left out, they follow CALL)."] [601 1 "// MonitoringEventName is event_names[ev]."] [609 1 "// MonitoringCall is call_one_instrument for the C API: tool's callback of ev called with args (0: none, or it returned;"] [610 1 "// 1: it returned DISABLE), with the thread's tracing count up. A native tool (the legacy profiler) has no callback for"] [611 1 "// an extension's events."] [635 1 "// MonitoringClearCallback clears tool's callback of ev (capi_call_instrumentation's \"Callback removed\")."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[104 41] [119 21] [159 29] [207 79] [208 29] [239 78] [252 40] [261 27] [265 36] [305 36] [319 25] [351 20] [408 29] [445 28] [462 22] [495 13] [495 29] [533 40] [553 40] [623 20]]} (go/file "monitoring.go" :imports [])

;; sys.monitoring's call-family events (PEP 669; queue 220, Python/instrumentation.c and Python/legacy_tracing.c of
;; CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement): the tools' registry (use_tool_id, free_tool_id, clear_tool_id, get_tool),
;; their global events (set_events, get_events) and callbacks (register_callback), and the events a profiler needs:
;; PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW, PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD, PY_UNWIND at a frame's start and end (runFrames), CALL, C_RETURN
;; and C_RAISE at the call sites of the loop and of compiled code (eval.go, aot.go). sys.setprofile is the legacy tool
;; over them (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID 6), as legacy_tracing.c makes it. _lsprof (builtins_lsprof.go) is a tool.
;;
;; Off, an event costs one load of monEvents (0 when no tool has an event) and a branch. A callback runs with the thread's
;; tracing count up (tstate->tracing): no event fires inside it. Not built: the local events (set_local_events,
;; get_local_events record nothing), LINE, INSTRUCTION, JUMP, BRANCH*, RAISE, RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED and
;; STOP_ITERATION never fire (settrace's are 219's). Since queue 274b a callback's DISABLE turns its event off at the
;; location for the tool (the code object and the offset; an event that cannot be disabled raises ValueError and loses
;; its callback), restart_events turns them on again, C_RETURN and C_RAISE follow CALL as CPython's ancillary events,
;; and sys.monitoring's C API (PyMonitoring_EnterScope, the _PyMonitoring_Fire*Event functions) is pyctypes' over
;; MonitoringTools and MonitoringCall below.
;; CALL's instruction_offset is 2 x the IR's instruction (f_lasti's unit).


